s://github.com/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf","homepage":"https://openairinterface.org/core-network/","size":20728,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"C++","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":15,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"collaborators_only","topics":["openairinterface-cn5g"],"visibility":"public","forks":1,"open_issues":15,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"develop","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/pulls/34","html_url":"https://github.com/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/pull/34","diff_url":"https://github.com/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/pull/34.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/pull/34.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Closes #33\n\n### Problem\n\nThe SM context reference counter starts at 0 on every SMF start, so a restarted SMF hands out references 1, 2, ... again. The AMF still holds references from the previous run. When it uses one of them, for example to release the SM context when a UE deregisters, the request reaches the SM context of another UE, and that UE loses its PDU session. Details and logs are in #33.\n\n### Change\n\n`smf_app` picks a random offset when it starts and adds it to every SM context reference. A reference from the previous run then finds no context, and the SMF answers 404 as for any unknown reference.\n\n- The offset is below 2^30, so the references stay below 2^31. The SMF parses them back with `std::stoi`.\n- `scid_t` and the generator in common-src are not changed.\n- Two runs can still give overlapping ranges, with a probability of about (number of contexts) / 2^30 for each restart. A counter persisted across restarts would remove that, but the SMF keeps no state on disk.\n\n### Testing\n\nLive, on an OAI RF simulator testbed: OAI gNB and 4 nrUEs, AMF and SMF v2.2.2 with local patches for stale UE contexts and stale PDU sessions (none changes SM context references), and UPF v2.2.2. The changed code is the same on `develop` and `v2.2.2`, so the commit was applied to the v2.2.2-based SMF for the test. Each run: restart the UPF and the SMF, restart UE A so that it gets the first new reference, then stop UE B, which holds the old reference with the same number.\n\n- **Without this change:** UE A got `sm-contexts/1`. When UE B was stopped, the AMF sent `sm-contexts/1/release`, the SMF released the session of UE A (HTTP 204), and UE A went from 3 of 3 pings to 0 of 3.\n- **With this change:** UE B held `sm-contexts/92996993` and UE A got `sm-contexts/713360807`. When UE B was stopped, the SMF answered the release with 404 (`Context associated with this id 0x58b0581 does not exit!`), and UE A kept 3 of 3 pings.\n- **Build:** `develop` with this commit builds (`docker/Dockerfile.smf.ubuntu`, target `oai-smf`, arm64) with no warning in the changed files. clang-format 19 gives no change.\n\n### Notes\n\n- This change does not make the AMF drop the contexts of a restarted SMF. TS 23.527 clause 6.1 leaves that clean-up to the implementation. The AMF can still send requests with old references; they now fail with 404 instead of reaching another UE.\n- When the UPF rejects the N4 Session Establishment, the SMF does not send `SMContextStatusNotify` (Release) (TS 23.502 clause 4.3.2.2.1 step 18), so the AMF keeps the reference. That is not changed here.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/issues/34/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openairinterface/oai-cn5g-smf/issues/34/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]